1. Scope and precedence

This is a source-available license, not an open-source license. It applies
only to original TenRiff material that its copyright holder first releases
under these terms, outside the exceptions below (the "Covered Material").
The licensor is the copyright holder granting rights in that material, or
their authorized representative, not automatically the repository owner.

The following exceptions take precedence over every restriction below:

(a) Previously licensed material. No existing MIT or other license grant is
    revoked or narrowed. In particular, the public snapshot at commit
    c6f6a3a817f63f59dab13dba8a87290288cd232d and earlier MIT releases remain
    available under MIT for their MIT-covered portions. The original MIT
    text and copyright notice are preserved in LICENSE-MIT. Their original
    third-party exceptions also remain. Anyone may continue to obtain, use,
    modify and redistribute those portions under those terms, including
    when the same material appears unchanged in a later version. A new
    filename, version number or license notice does not remove those rights.
    Material previously licensed permissively elsewhere is also excluded.

(b) Third-party and separately licensed material. Existing file-level and
    component licenses, copyright notices, patent grants, source-offer
    obligations and attribution requirements remain in force. See
    THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and each component's notices. This includes
    external/, third_party/, nk2e/, nk2eplus/, and the Apache-2.0-licensed
    src/gameplay/KeyModeConverter.cpp and src/gameplay/KeyModeConverter.h.
    This license grants no additional rights in another person's work and
    imposes no additional restrictions on rights granted by its license.
    Separately licensed material keeps its license when copied elsewhere.

(c) Permissive project materials. Original project contributions in docs/,
    examples/, skins/, assets/, Mainmusic/, config/, models/, and
    tools/skin_editor/, plus launch_skin_editor.bat, remain under LICENSE-MIT,
    unless a more specific license or third-party notice applies. This
    permission is given only by contributors entitled to grant it. It does
    not claim ownership of third-party music, charts, fonts, models or art.

Subject to these exceptions, the default for new original engine/game code,
tests, development tools and build scripts first released with this policy
is this license. Merely placing an old contribution in such a path does not
relicense it. For a file containing both earlier permissive code and new
Covered Material, these terms apply only to the new Covered Material.

2. Permissions without a separate agreement

Subject to retaining applicable notices, you may, without a license fee:

(a) View, download and keep copies of the Covered Material for private study
    and evaluation, and build and run unmodified source for your own use.
(b) Install and run official TenRiff binaries for gameplay and operate an
    unmodified TenRiff multiplayer server. These permissions do not depend
    on whether gameplay, an event or a gameplay recording earns revenue.
(c) Share complete, unmodified official binary release packages without
    charging for the package, preserving this license and all applicable
    third-party notices and required source materials or source offers.
(d) Create, use and distribute independently authored charts, skins,
    configurations and tools using the documented formats/interfaces. Your
    original creations and game output are not subject to this license
    merely because they work with TenRiff. Third-party content still needs
    its own permission. Reusing Covered Material in a tool is not authorized
    by this paragraph.
(e) Publish gameplay screenshots, videos, streams, reviews and commentary,
    including monetized content, to the extent the licensor owns the rights.
(f) Make changes solely to prepare a contribution to TenRiff and submit that
    contribution through this repository's review process. Hosting the
    corresponding review branch and patch for that purpose is permitted.
    This does not permit distributing a separate modified game or product.

Rights granted by GitHub's applicable Terms of Service, including public
repository viewing and forking, are not restricted by this license. Such
forking does not by itself grant any additional right to reuse Covered
Material outside those terms and the permissions above.

3. Uses requiring prior written permission

Except as permitted in section 2 or by an exception in section 1, you must
obtain prior written permission from the relevant copyright holder(s) to:

(a) Copy or incorporate Covered Material into another project or product.
(b) Modify, adapt, port, translate or otherwise create derivative works of
    Covered Material.
(c) Redistribute Covered Material as source or binaries, including modified
    versions, or sell, sublicense or commercially license it.

These requirements apply to both commercial and noncommercial reuse. A
copyright notice or credit alone is not permission. No blanket commercial
reuse license is granted. All rights not expressly granted are reserved.
Nothing here restricts uses allowed by applicable law, including copyright
exceptions, or any third-party license rights (including LGPL modification,
replacement, relinking and reverse-engineering rights where applicable).

4. Permission requests and contributions

Request permission at https://github.com/10kseason/TenRiff/issues using the
subject "License permission request", identifying the files/version, intended
use, modifications and distribution. Do not post confidential information.
The repository maintainer can grant permission only for rights they own or
are authorized to license. Silence or issue closure is not approval. Written
permission must explicitly identify the authorized use and relevant rights.

Contributors retain ownership. Submit new original contributions under the
terms applicable to their destination, and identify any separately licensed
material. No copyright assignment, retroactive relicensing or authority to
relicense somebody else's contribution is implied by accepting a patch.
By intentionally submitting new Covered Material for inclusion in TenRiff,
you grant its maintainers a nonexclusive, worldwide, royalty-free permission
to use, reproduce, modify and distribute your contribution as part of
official TenRiff source and binary releases under this license. This grant
does not authorize them to remove third-party terms or relicense your
contribution under unrelated terms. Separately licensed submissions retain
their stated terms instead.

